  "body": "As discussed recently on blink-dev, these dialogs are often used for\nscams and such. At least Chrome has already applied the mitigation\nstrategy of limiting the length of the author-supplied text to 2K\ncharacters (and @avidrissman proposes that Chrome limit it further). We\nshould call out in the spec that this is explicitly allowed, like we\nalready do for the beforeunload text.\n\nhttps://groups.google.com/a/chromium.org/forum/#!topic/blink-dev/cFtsKXKd4F0\nhas some background.\n## \n\nCurious if any other browsers also have limits in place already. (I tried poking around Gecko code but didn't see anything.) Regardless, I think this is a shoe-in for merging since the spec already allows such implementer freedom around these dialogs, and because we already allow truncation for beforeunload dialogs.\n",
